            "contentType": "VIDEO",
            "title": "Meme stocks vs. crypto: How retail investors are trading",
            "description": "<p>Robinhood (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:1;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/HOOD\">HOOD</a>) chief investment officer Stephanie Guild joins Opening Bid to discuss how retail investors are trading crypto and meme stocks, like Opendoor (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:2;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/OPEN\">OPEN</a>) and Better Home & Finance (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:3;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/BETR\">BETR</a>).</p>\n<p>The focus on meme stocks and crypto comes as gold (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:4;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/GC=F\">GC=F</a>) is trading near record highs. Yahoo Finance Senior Reporter <a data-i13n=\"cpos:5;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/author/ines-ferre/\">Ines Ferr\u00e9</a> outlines the move in the commodity price, which is typically a risk-off trade.</p>\n<p>To watch more expert insights and analysis on the latest market action, check out more <a data-i13n=\"cpos:6;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/videos/series/opening-bid/\">Opening Bid</a>.</p>",
